WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.630
Everything about this snowflake began with a triangle.

00:00:03.680 --> 00:00:06.150
Three sides, three corners.

00:00:06.200 --> 00:00:09.510
Now look at the finished shape, and count its arms.

00:00:09.560 --> 00:00:10.470
Six.

00:00:10.520 --> 00:00:16.470
The same rule, the same triangle, and somewhere along the way, three became six.

00:00:16.520 --> 00:00:18.570
You start with a triangle.

00:00:18.620 --> 00:00:20.530
So why six arms?

00:00:20.580 --> 00:00:29.270
In this mission, you'll meet two kinds of symmetry: folding a shape along a mirror line, and turning it about its centre until it matches itself.

00:00:29.320 --> 00:00:40.890
You'll test the snowflake's symmetry, zoom right in on its edge for a surprise, and meet the mathematician who published this curve, over a hundred years ago, and find out why he built it.

00:00:40.940 --> 00:00:45.480
Your mission: explain why a triangle ends up with six arms.
